title: VMware Aria Automation: Cluster wide service
agents: aria_automation
catalog: app/vmware
license: GPLv2
distribution: kuhn-ruess
description:
 Monitors the cluster wide state of an Aria Automation service, taken from
 '/api/v1/services/cluster'. The special agent sends these services as
 piggyback data to the host set in the rule, or creates them on each node
 host without that option.

 The state is {OK} if the service is "started", {CRIT} otherwise. The health
 is mapped like for the node services ("healthy" {OK}, "degraded"/"warning"
 {WARN}, "unknown" {UNKN}, anything else {CRIT}). The number of instances and
 their nodes are shown; every instance that is not "running" or not
 "healthy" adds a {WARN} with its node. No instance at all is {CRIT}.

item:
 The name of the Aria Automation service.

discovery:
 One service per service of the cluster.
